(function(){if(!window.__hermes_register_book)return;window.__hermes_register_book("alc1-c",[{"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Son of Cleinias, I think it must surprise you that I, the first of all your lovers, am the only one of them who has not given up his suit and thrown you over, and whereas they have all pestered you with their conversation I have not spoken one word to you for so many years. The cause of this has been nothing human, but a certain spiritual opposition, of whose power you shall be informed at some later time. However, it now opposes me no longer, so I have accordingly come to you; and I am in good hopes that it will not oppose me again in the future. Now I have been observing you all this time, and have formed a pretty good notion of your behavior to your lovers: for although they were many and high-spirited, everyone of them has found your spirit too strong for him and has run away.", "st": "103a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Let me explain the reason of your spirit being too much for them. You say you have no need of any man in any matter; for your resources are so great, beginning with the body and ending with the soul, that you lack nothing. You think, in the first place, that you are foremost in beauty and stature—and you are not mistaken in this, as is plain for all to see—and in the second place, that you are of the most gallant family in your city, the greatest city in Greece, and that there you have, through your father, very many of the best people as your friends and kinsmen, who would assist you in case of need, and other connections also, through your mother, who are not a whit inferior to these, nor fewer. And you reckon upon a stronger power than all those that I have mentioned, in Pericles, son of Xanthippus, whom your father left as guardian of you and your brother when he died, and who is able to do whatever he likes not only in this city but all over Greece and among many great nations of the barbarians. And I will add besides the wealth of your house: but on this, I observe, you presume least of all. Well, you puff yourself up on all these advantages, and have overcome your lovers, while they in their inferiority have yielded to your might, and all this has not escaped you; so I am very sure that you wonder what on earth I mean by not getting rid of my passion, and what can be my hope in remaining when the rest have fled.", "st": "104a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Perhaps also, Socrates, you are not aware that you have only just anticipated me. For I, in fact, had the intention of coming and asking you first that very same question—what is your aim and expectation in bothering me by making a particular point of always turning up wherever I may be. For I really do wonder what can be your object, and should be very glad if you would tell me.", "st": "104c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you will listen to me, presumably, with keen attention if, as you say, you long to know what I mean, and I have in you a listener who will stay to hear me out.", "st": "104d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, to be sure: only speak."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Look to it, then; for it would be no wonder if I should make as much difficulty about stopping as I have made about starting.", "st": "104e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> My good sir, speak; for I will listen."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Speak I must, I suppose. Now, although it is hard for a lover to parley with a man who does not yield to lovers, I must make bold nevertheless to put my meaning into words. For if I saw you, Alcibiades, content with the things I set forth just now, and minded to pass your life in enjoying them, I should long ago have put away my love, so at least I persuade myself: but as it is, I shall propound to your face quite another set of your thoughts, whereby you will understand that I have had you continually before my mind. For I believe, if some god should ask you: Alcibiades, do you prefer to live with your present possessions, or to die immediately if you are not to have the chance of acquiring greater things? I believe you would choose to die. But let me tell you what I imagine must be the present hope of your life. You think that if you come shortly before the Athenian Assembly—which you expect to occur in a very few days—you will stand forth and prove to the people that you are more worthy of honor than either Pericles or anyone else who has ever existed, and that having proved this you will have the greatest power in the state; and that if you are the greatest here, you will be the same among all the other Greeks, and not only Greeks, but all the barbarians who inhabit the same continent with us. And if that same god should say to you again, that you are to hold sway here in Europe, but are not to be allowed to cross over into Asia and to interfere with the affairs of that region, I believe you would be equally loth to live on those sole conditions either—if you are not to fill, one may say, the whole world with your name and your power; and I fancy that, except Cyrus and Xerxes, you think there has never existed a single man who was of any account. So then that this is your hope, I know well enough; I am not merely guessing. And I daresay you will reply, since you know that what I say is true: Well, Socrates, and what has that to do with your point? I am going to tell you, dear son of Cleinias and Deinomache. Without me it is impossible for all those designs of yours to be crowned with achievement; so great is the power I conceive myself to have over your affairs and over you, and it is for this very reason, I believe, that the god has so long prevented me from talking with you, and I was waiting to see when he would allow me. For as you have hopes of proving yourself in public to be invaluable to the state and, having proved it, of winning forthwith unlimited power, so do I hope to win supreme power over you by proving that I am invaluable to you, and that neither guardian nor kinsman nor anyone else is competent to transmit to you the power that you long for except me, with the god’s help, however. In your younger days, to be sure, before you had built such high hopes, the god, as I believe, prevented me from talking with you, in order that I might not waste my words: but now he has set me on; for now you will listen to me.", "st": "105a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You seem to me far more extraordinary, Socrates, now that you have begun to speak, than before, when you followed me about in silence; though even then you looked strange enough. Well, as to my intending all this or not, you have apparently made your decision, and any denial of mine will not avail me to persuade you. Very good: but supposing I have intended ever so much what you say, how are you the sole means through which I can hope to attain it? Can you tell me?", "st": "106a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Are you asking whether I can make a long speech, such as you are used to hearing? No, my gift is not of that sort. But I fancy I could prove to you that the case is so, if you will consent to do me just one little service.", "st": "106b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, if you mean a service that is not troublesome, I consent."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you consider it troublesome to answer questions put to you?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, I do not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then answer."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Ask."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, you have the intentions which I say you have, I suppose?", "st": "106c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Be it so, if you like, in order that I may know what you will say next."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now then: you intend, as I say, to come forward as adviser to the Athenians in no great space of time; well, suppose I were to take hold of you as you were about to ascend the platform, and were to ask you: Alcibiades, on what subject do the Athenians propose to take advice, that you should stand up to advise them? Is it something about which you have better knowledge than they? What would be your reply?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I should say, I suppose, it was something about which I knew better than they.", "st": "106d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you are a good adviser on things about which you actually know."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you know only the things you have learnt from others or discovered yourself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What could I know besides?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And can it be that you would ever have learnt or discovered anything without being willing either to learn it or to inquire into it yourself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, would you have been willing to inquire into or learn what you thought you knew?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So there was a time when you did not think that you knew what you now actually know.", "st": "106e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> There must have been."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, but I know pretty nearly the things that you have learnt: tell me if anything has escaped me. You learnt, if I recollect, writing and harping and wrestling; as for fluting, you refused to learn it. These are the things that you know, unless perhaps there is something you have been learning unobserved by me; and this you were not, I believe, if you so much as stepped out of doors either by night or by day."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, I have taken no other lessons than those."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then tell me, will it be when the Athenians are taking advice how they are to do their writing correctly that you are to stand up and advise them?", "st": "107a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Upon my word, not I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, about strokes on the lyre?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Not at all."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor in fact are they accustomed to deliberate on throws in wrestling either at the Assembly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, to be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what will be the subject of the advice? For I presume it will not be about building."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For a builder will give better advice than you in that matter.", "st": "107b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor yet will it be about divination?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For there again a diviner will serve better than you."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Whether he be short or tall, handsome or ugly, nay, noble or ignoble."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For on each subject the advice comes from one who knows, not one who has riches."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And whether their mentor be poor or rich will make no difference to the Athenians when they deliberate for the health of the citizens; all that they require of their counsellor is that he be a physician.", "st": "107c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Naturally."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what will they have under consideration if you are to be right in standing up, when you do so, as their counsellor?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Their own affairs, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you mean with regard to shipbuilding, and the question as to what sort of ships they ought to get built?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, I do not, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because, I imagine, you do not understand shipbuilding. Is that, and that alone, the reason?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is just the reason."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, on what sort of affairs of their own do you mean that they will be deliberating?", "st": "107d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> On war, Socrates, or on peace, or on any other of the state’s affairs."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you mean that they will be deliberating with whom they ought to make peace, and on whom they ought to make war, and in what manner?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And on whom it is better to do so, ought they not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And at such time as it is better?", "st": "107e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And for so long as they had better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now if the Athenians should deliberate with whom they should wrestle close, and with whom only at arm’s length, and in what manner, would you or the wrestling-master be the better adviser?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> The wrestling-master, I presume."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And can you tell me what the wrestling-master would have in view when he advised as to the persons with whom they ought or ought not to wrestle close, and when and in what manner? What I mean is something like this: ought they not to wrestle close with those with whom it is better to do so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so far as is better, too?", "st": "108a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> So far."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And at such time also as is better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But again, when one sings, one has sometimes to accompany the song with harping and stepping?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, one has."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And at such time as is better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so far as is better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, since you applied the term better to the two cases of harping for accompaniment of a song and close wrestling, what do you call the better in the case of harping, to correspond with what in the case of wrestling I call gymnastic? What do you call the other?", "st": "108b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do not understand."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, try to copy me: for my answer gave you, I think, what is correct in every instance; and that is correct, I presume, which proceeds by rule of the art, is it not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And was not the art here gymnastic?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I said that the better in the case of wrestling was gymnastic.", "st": "108c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You did."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I was quite fair?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come then, in your turn—for it would befit you also, I fancy, to argue fairly —tell me, first, what is the art which includes harping and singing and treading the measure correctly? What is it called as a whole? You cannot yet tell me?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, try another way: who are the goddesses that foster the art?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> The Muses, you mean, Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I do. Now, just think, and say by what name the art is called after them.", "st": "108d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Music, I suppose you mean."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes, I do. And what is that which proceeds correctly by its rule? As in the other case I was correct in mentioning to you gymnastic as that which goes by the art, so I ask you, accordingly, what you say in this case. What manner of proceeding is required?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> A musical one, I suppose."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> You are right. Come then, what is it that you term better, in respect of what is better in waging war and being at peace? Just as in our other instances you said that the better implied the more musical and again, in the parallel case, the more gymnastical, try now if you can tell me what is the better in this case.", "st": "108e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But I am quite unable."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But surely that is disgraceful; for if you should speak to somebody as his adviser on food, and say that one sort was better than another, at this time and in this quantity, and he then asked you—What do you mean by the better, Alcibiades?—in a matter like that you could tell him you meant the more wholesome, although you do not set up to be a physician; yet in a case where you set up to have knowledge and are ready to stand up and advise as though you knew, are you not ashamed to be unable, as appears, to answer a question upon it? Does it not seem disgraceful?", "st": "109a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Very."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then consider and do your best to tell me the connection of better in being at peace or at war with those to whom we ought to be so disposed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, I am considering, but I fail to perceive it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But you must know what treatment it is that we allege against each other when we enter upon a war, and what name we give it when we do so?", "st": "109b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do: we say we are victims of deceit or violence or spoliation."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Enough: how do we suffer each of these things? Try and tell me what difference there is between one way and another."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Do you mean by that, Socrates, whether it is in a just way or an unjust way?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Precisely."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, there you have all the difference in the world."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, on which sort are you going to advise the Athenians to make war—those who are acting unjustly, or those who are doing what is just?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is a hard question: for even if someone decides that he must go to war with those who are doing what is just, he would not admit that they were doing so.", "st": "109c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For that would not be lawful, I suppose?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed; nor is it considered honorable either."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you too will appeal to these things in making your speeches?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Necessarily."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then must not that better about which I was asking in reference to making or not making war, on those on whom we ought to or not, and when we ought to or not, be simply and solely the juster?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently it is."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> How now, friend Alcibiades? Have you overlooked your own ignorance of this matter, or have I overlooked your learning it and taking lessons of a master who taught you to distinguish the more just and the more unjust? And who is he? Inform me in my turn, in order that you may introduce me to him as another pupil.", "st": "109d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You are joking, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> No, I swear by our common God of Friendship, whose name I would by no means take in vain. Come, if you can, tell me who the man is.", "st": "109e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But what if I cannot? Do you think I could not know about what is just and unjust in any other way?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes, you might, supposing you discovered it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But do you not think I might discover it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes, quite so, if you inquired."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> And do you not think I might inquire?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I do, if you thought you did not know."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> And was there not a time when I held that view?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well spoken. Then can you tell me at what time it was that you thought you did not know what is just and unjust? Pray, was it a year ago that you were inquiring, and thought you did not know? Or did you think you knew? Please answer truly, that our debates may not be futile.", "st": "110a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, I thought I knew."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And two years, and three years, and four years back, were you not of the same mind?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I was."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But, you see, before that time you were a child, were you not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So I know well enough that then you thought you knew."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How do you know it so well?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Many a time I heard you, when as a child you were dicing or playing some other game at your teacher’s or elsewhere, instead of showing hesitation about what was just and unjust, speak in very loud and confident tones about one or other of your playmates, saying he was a rascal and a cheat who played unfairly. Is not this a true account?", "st": "110b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But what was I to do, Socrates, when somebody cheated me?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yet if you were ignorant then whether you were being unfairly treated or not, how can you ask— What are you to do?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, but on my word, I was not ignorant: no, I clearly understood that I was being wronged.", "st": "110c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you thought you knew, even as a child, it seems, what was just and unjust."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I did; and I knew too."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> At what sort of time did you discover it? For surely it was not while you thought you knew."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then when did you think you were ignorant? Consider; I believe you will fail to find such a time."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Upon my word, Socrates, I really cannot say."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you do not know it by discovery.", "st": "110d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Not at all, apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But you said just now that you did not know it by learning either; and if you neither discovered nor learnt it, how do you come to know it, and whence?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, perhaps that answer I gave you was not correct, that I knew it by my own discovery."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then how was it done?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I learnt it, I suppose, in the same way as everyone else."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Back we come to the same argument. From whom? Please tell me."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> From the many.", "st": "110e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> They are no very serious teachers with whom you take refuge, if you ascribe it to the many!"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, are they not competent to teach?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Not how to play, or not to play, draughts; and yet that, I imagine, is a slight matter compared with justice. What? Do you not think so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then if they are unable to teach the slighter, can they teach the more serious matter?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think so: at any rate, there are many other things that they are able to teach, more serious than draughts."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> What sort of things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> For instance, it was from them that I learnt to speak Greek, and I could not say who was my teacher, but can only ascribe it to the same people who, you say, are not serious teachers.", "st": "111a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Ah, gallant sir, the many may be good teachers of that, and they can justly be praised for their teaching of such subjects."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> And why?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because in those subjects they have the equipment proper to good teachers."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What do you mean by that?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> You know that those who are going to teach anything should first know it themselves, do you not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course.", "st": "111b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And that those who know should agree with each other and not differ?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But if they differ upon anything, will you say that they know it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then how can they be teachers of it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By no means."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, do you find that the many differ about the nature of stone or wood? If you ask one of them, do they not agree on the same answer, and make for the same things when they want to get a piece of stone or wood? It is just the same, too, with everything of the sort: for I am pretty nearly right in understanding you to mean just this by knowing how to speak Greek, am I not?", "st": "111c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And on these matters, as we stated, they not only agree with each other and with themselves in private, but states also use in public the same terms about them to each other, without any dispute?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> They do."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then naturally they will be good teachers of these matters.", "st": "111d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if we should wish to provide anyone with knowledge of them, we should be right in sending him to be taught by the many that you speak of?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But what if we wished to know not only what men were like or what horses were like, but which of them were good runners or not? Would the many still suffice to teach us this?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you have ample proof that they do not know this, and are not proficient teachers of it, in their not agreeing about it at all with themselves?", "st": "111e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I have."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what if we wished to know not only what men were like, but what healthy or diseased men were like? Would the many suffice to teach us?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you would have proof of their being bad teachers of that, if you saw them differing about it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I should."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, do you now find that the many agree with themselves or each other about just and unjust men or things?", "st": "112a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Far from it, on my word, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> In fact, they differ most especially on these points?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Very much so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I suppose you never yet saw or heard of people differing so sharply on questions of health or the opposite as to fight and kill one another in battle because of them."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But on questions of justice or injustice I am sure you have; and if you have not seen them, at any rate you have heard of them from many people, especially Homer. For you have heard the Odyssey and the Iliad?", "st": "112b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I certainly have, I suppose, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And these poems are about a difference of just and unjust"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And from this difference arose the fights and deaths of the Achaeans, and of the Trojans as well, and of the suitors of Penelope in their strife with Odysseus."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true.", "st": "112c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I imagine that when the Athenians and Spartans and Boeotians lost their men at Tanagra, and later at Coronea, among whom your own father perished, the difference that caused their deaths and fights was solely on a question of just and unjust, was it not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then are we to say that these people understand those questions, on which they differ so sharply that they are led by their mutual disputes to take these extreme measures against each other?", "st": "112d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you refer me to teachers of that sort, whom you admit yourself to be without knowledge?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems I do."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then how is it likely that you should know what is just and unjust, when you are so bewildered about these matters and are shown to have neither learnt them from anyone nor discovered them for yourself?."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By what you say, it is not likely."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> There again, Alcibiades, do you see how unfairly you speak?", "st": "112e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> In what?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> In stating that I say so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, do you not say that l do not know about the just and unjust?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Not at all."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, do I say it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How, pray?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I will show you, in the following way. If I ask you which is the greater number, one or two, you will answer two?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, I shall."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> How much greater?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By one."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then which of us says that two are one more than one?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I was asking, and you were answering?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then is it I, the questioner, or you the answerer, that are found to be speaking about these things?", "st": "113a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what if I ask what are the letters in Socrates, and you tell me? Which will be the speaker?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come then, tell me, as a principle, when we have question and answer, which is the speaker—the questioner, or the answerer?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> The answerer, I should say, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And throughout the argument so far, I was the questioner?", "st": "113b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you the answerer?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, which of us has spoken what has been said?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently, Socrates, from what we have admitted, it was I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And it was said that Alcibiades, the fair son of Cleinias, did not know about just and unjust, but thought he did, and intended to go to the Assembly as adviser to the Athenians on what he knows nothing about; is not that so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently.", "st": "113c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then, to quote Euripides, the result is, Alcibiades, that you may be said to have heard it from yourself, not me, and it is not I who say it, but you, and you tax me with it in vain. And indeed what you say is quite true. For it is a mad scheme this, that you meditate, my excellent friend—of teaching things that you do not know, since you have taken no care to learn them."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think, Socrates, that the Athenians and the rest of the Greeks rarely deliberate as to which is the more just or unjust course: for they regard questions of this sort as obvious; and so they pass them over and consider which course will prove more expedient in the result. For the just and the expedient, I take it, are not the same, but many people have profited by great wrongs that they have committed, whilst others, I imagine, have had no advantage from doing what was right.", "st": "113d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> What then? Granting that the just and the expedient are in fact as different as they can be, you surely do not still suppose you know what is expedient for mankind, and why it is so?", "st": "113e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, what is the obstacle, Socrates,—unless you are going to ask me again from whom I learnt it, or how I discovered it for myself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> What a way of going on! If your answer is incorrect, and a previous argument can be used to prove it so, you claim to be told something new, and a different line of proof, as though the previous one were like a poor worn-out coat which you refuse to wear any longer; you must be provided instead with something clean and unsoiled in the way of evidence. But I shall ignore your sallies in debate, and shall none the less ask you once more, where you learnt your knowledge of what is expedient, and who is your teacher, asking in one question all the things I asked before; and now you will clearly find yourself in the same plight, and will be unable to prove that you know the expedient either through discovery or through learning. But as you are dainty, and would dislike a repeated taste of the same argument, I pass over this question of whether you know or do not know what is expedient for the Athenians: but why have you not made it clear whether the just and the expedient are the same or different? If you like, question me as I did you, or if you prefer, argue out the matter in your own way.", "st": "114a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But I am not sure I should be able, Socrates, to set it forth to you.", "st": "114b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, my good sir, imagine I am the people in Assembly; even there, you know, you will have to persuade each man singly, will you not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the same man may well persuade one person singly, and many together, about things that he knows, just as the schoolmaster, I suppose, persuades either one or many about letters?", "st": "114c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And again, will not the same man persuade either one or many about number?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And this will be the man who knows—the arithmetician?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you too can persuade a single man about things of which you can persuade many?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Presumably."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And these are clearly things that you know."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the only difference between the orator speaking before the people and one who speaks in a conversation like ours is that the former persuades men in a number together of the same things, and the latter persuades them one at a time?", "st": "114d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It looks like it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come now, since we see that the same man may persuade either many or one, try your unpracticed hand on me, and endeavor to show that the just is sometimes not expedient."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You are insolent, Socrates!"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> This time, at any rate, I am going to have the insolence to persuade you of the opposite of that which you decline to prove to me."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Speak, then."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Just answer my questions."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, you yourself must be the speaker.", "st": "114e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> What? Do you not wish above all things to be persuaded?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By all means, to be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you would best be persuaded if you should say the case is so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then answer; and if you do not hear your own self say that the just is expedient, put no trust in the words of anyone again."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I will not: but I may as well answer; for I do not think I shall come to any harm."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> You are quite a prophet! Now tell me, do you consider some just things to be expedient, and others not?", "st": "115a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And again, some noble, and some not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What do you mean by that question?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I would ask whether anyone ever seemed to you to be doing what was base and yet just."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Never."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, are all just things noble?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what of noble things, in their turn? Are they all good, or some only, while others are not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> In my opinion, Socrates, some noble things are evil."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And some base things are good?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you mean as in one of the many cases where men have gone to rescue a comrade or kinsman in battle, and have been either wounded or killed, while those who did not go to the rescue, as duty bade, have got off safe and sound?", "st": "115b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Precisely."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And such a rescue you call noble, in respect of the endeavor to save those whom it was one’s duty to save; and this is courage, is it not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But you call it evil, in respect of the deaths and wounds?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And is not the courage one thing, and the death another?", "st": "115c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then it is not in the same respect that rescuing one’s friends is noble and evil?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then see if, inasmuch as it is noble, it is also good; for in the present case you were admitting that the rescue was noble in respect of its courage: now consider this very thing, courage, and say whether it is good or bad. Consider it in this way: which would you choose to have, good things or evil?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And most of all, the greatest goods, and of such things you would least allow yourself to be deprived?", "st": "115d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what do you say of courage? At what price would you allow yourself to be deprived of it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I would give up life itself if I had to be a coward."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you regard cowardice as the uttermost evil."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> On a par with death, it seems."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And life and courage are the extreme opposites of death and cowardice?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you would most desire to have the former, and least the latter?", "st": "115e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Is that because you think the former best, and the latter worst?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you reckon courage among the best things, and death among the worst."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then the rescue of one’s friends in battle, inasmuch as it is noble in respect of the working of good by courage, you have termed noble?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But evil, in respect of the working of evil by death?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So we may fairly describe each of these workings as follows: as you call either of them evil because of the evil it produces, so you must call it good because of the good it produces.", "st": "116a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I believe that is so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And again, are they noble inasmuch as they are good, and base inasmuch as they are evil?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then in saying that the rescue of one’s friends in battle is noble and yet evil, you mean just the same as if you called the rescue good, but evil."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I believe what you say is true, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So nothing noble, in so far as it is noble, is evil, and nothing base, in so far as it is base, is good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently.", "st": "116b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now then, consider it again in this way: whoever does nobly, does well too, does he not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And are not those who do well happy?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And they are happy because of the acquisition of good things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And they acquire these by doing well and nobly?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So doing well is good?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And welfare is noble?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Hence we have seen again that noble and good are the same thing.", "st": "116c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then whatever we find to be noble we shall find also to be good, by this argument at least."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> We must."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, are good things expedient or not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Expedient."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And do you remember what our admissions were about just things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think we said that those who do just things must do noble things."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And that those who do noble things must do good things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And that good things are expedient?", "st": "116d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Hence just things, Alcibiades, are expedient."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> So it seems."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, are not you the speaker of all this, and I the questioner?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I seem to be, apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So if anyone stands up to advise either the Athenians or the Peparethians, imagining that he understands what is just and unjust, and says that just things are sometimes evil, could you do other than laugh him to scorn, since you actually say yourself that just and expedient are the same?", "st": "116e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But by Heaven, Socrates, I do not even know what I am saying, I feel altogether in such a strange state! For from moment to moment I change my view under your questioning."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And are you unaware, my friend, what this feeling is?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I am, quite."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, do you suppose that if someone should ask you whether you have two eyes or three, two hands or four, or anything else of that sort, you would answer differently from moment to moment, or always the same thing?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I begin to have misgivings about myself, but still I think I should make the same answer.", "st": "117a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the reason would be, because you know?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then if you involuntarily give contradictory answers, clearly it must be about things of which you are ignorant."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Very likely."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you say you are bewildered in answering about just and unjust, noble and base, evil and good, expedient and inexpedient? Now, is it not obvious that your bewilderment is caused by your ignorance of these things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree.", "st": "117b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then is it the case that when a man does not know a thing he must needs be bewildered in spirit regarding that thing?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, do you know in what way you can ascend to heaven?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> On my word, not I."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Is that too a kind of question about which your judgement is bewildered?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you know the reason, or shall I state it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> State it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> It is, my friend, that while not knowing the matter you do not suppose that you know it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Here again, how do you mean?", "st": "117c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do your share, in seeing for yourself. Are you bewildered about the kind of thing that you do not know and are aware of not knowing? For instance, you know, I suppose, that you do not know about the preparation of a tasty dish?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then do you think for yourself how you are to prepare it, and get bewildered, or do you entrust it to the person who knows?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do the latter."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what if you should be on a ship at sea? Would you think whether the tiller should be moved inwards or outwards, and in your ignorance bewilder yourself, or would you entrust it to the helmsman, and be quiet?", "st": "117d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I would leave it to him."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you are not bewildered about what you do not know, so long as you know that you do not know?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems I am not,"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then do you note that mistakes in action also are due to this ignorance of thinking one knows when one does not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Here again, how do you mean?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> We set about acting, I suppose, when we think we know what we are doing?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes.", "st": "117e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But when people think they do not know, I suppose they hand it over to others?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so that kind of ignorant person makes no mistakes in life, because they entrust such matters to others?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Who then are those who make mistakes? For, I take it, they cannot be those who know."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But since it is neither those who know, nor those of the ignorant who know that they do not know, the only people left, I think, are those who do not know, but think that they do?", "st": "118a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, only those."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then this ignorance is a cause of evils, and is the discreditable sort of stupidity?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And when it is about the greatest matters, it is most injurious and base?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By far."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, can you mention any greater things than the just, the noble, the good, and the expedient?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And it is about these, you say, that you are bewildered?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But if you are bewildered, is it not clear from what has gone before that you are not only ignorant of the greatest things, but while not knowing them you think that you do?", "st": "118b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I am afraid so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Alack then, Alcibiades, for the plight you are in! I shrink indeed from giving it a name, but still, as we are alone, let me speak out. You are wedded to stupidity, my fine friend, of the vilest kind; you are impeached of this by your own words, out of your own mouth; and this, it seems, is why you dash into politics before you have been educated. And you are not alone in this plight, but you share it with most of those who manage our city’s affairs, except just a few, and perhaps your guardian, Pericles.", "st": "118c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, you know, Socrates, they say he did not get his wisdom independently, but consorted with many wise men, such as Pythocleides and Anaxagoras; and now, old as he is, he still confers with Damon for that very purpose."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, but did you ever find a man who was wise in anything and yet unable to make another man wise in the same things as himself? For instance, the man who taught you letters was wise himself, and also made you wise, and anyone else he wished to, did he not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you too, who learnt from him, will be able to make another man wise?", "st": "118d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the same holds of the harper and the trainer?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For, I presume, it is a fine proof of one’s knowing anything that one knows, when one is able to point to another man whom one has made to know it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, can you tell me whom Pericles made wise? One of his sons, to begin with?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But what if the two sons of Pericles were simpletons, Socrates?", "st": "118e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, Cleinias, your brother."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But why should you mention Cleinias, a madman?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, if Cleinias is mad and the two sons of Pericles were simpletons, what reason are we to assign, in your case, for his allowing you to be in your present condition?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I believe I am myself to blame for not attending to him."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But tell me of any other Athenian or foreigner, slave or freeman, who is accounted to have become wiser through converse with Pericles; as I can tell you that Pythodorus son of Isolochus, and Callias, son of Calliades, became through that of Zeno; each of them has paid Zeno a hundred minae, and has become both wise and distinguished.", "st": "119a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, upon my word, I cannot."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Very good: then what is your intention regarding yourself? Will you remain as you are, or take some trouble?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> We must put our heads together, Socrates. And indeed, as soon as you speak, I take the point and agree. For the men who manage the city’s affairs, apart from a few, do strike me as uneducated.", "st": "119b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what does that mean?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That if they were educated, I suppose anyone who undertook to contend against them would have to get some knowledge and practice first, as he would for a match with athletes: but now, seeing that these men have gone in for politics as amateurs, what need is there for me to practise and have the trouble of learning? For I am sure that my natural powers alone will give me an easy victory over them.", "st": "119c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Ho, ho, my good sir, what a thing to say! How unworthy of your looks and your other advantages!"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is your meaning now, Socrates? What is the connection?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I am grieved for you, and for my love."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, pray?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> That you should expect your contest to be with the men we have here."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, but with whom is it to be?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Is that a worthy question to be asked by a man who considers himself high-spirited?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How do you mean? Is not my contest with these men?", "st": "119d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, suppose you were intending to steer a warship into action, would you be content to be the best hand among the crew at steering or, while regarding this skill as a necessary qualification, would you keep your eye on your actual opponents in the fight, and not, as now, on your fellow-fighters? These, I conceive, you ought so far to surpass that they would not feel fit to be your opponents, but only to be your despised fellow-fighters against the enemy, if you mean really to make your mark with some noble action that will be worthy both of yourself and of the city.", "st": "119e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, I do mean to."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So you think it quite fitting for you to be satisfied if you are better than the soldiers, but neglect to keep your eye on the enemy’s leaders with a view to showing yourself better than they are, or to plan and practise against them!"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of whom are you speaking now, Socrates?", "st": "120a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you not know that our city makes war occasionally on the Spartans and on the Great King?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if you are minded to be the head of our state, you would be right in thinking that your contest is with the kings of Sparta and of Persia?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That sounds like the truth."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> No, my good friend; you ought rather to keep your eye on Meidias the quail-filliper and others of his sort—who undertake to manage the city’s affairs, while they still have the slavish hair (as the women would say) showing in their minds through their lack of culture, and have not yet got rid of it; who, moreover, have come with their outlandish speech to flatter the state, not to rule it—to these, I tell you, should your eyes be turned; and then you can disregard yourself, and need neither learn what is to be learnt for the great contest in which you are to be engaged, nor practise what requires practice, and so ensure that you are perfectly prepared before entering upon a political career.", "st": "120b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, Socrates, I believe you are right; though I think neither the Spartan generals nor the Persian king are at all different from other people.", "st": "120c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But, my excellent friend, consider what this notion of yours means."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> In regard to what?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> First of all, do you think you would take more pains over yourself if you feared them and thought them terrible, or if you did not?", "st": "120d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly, if I thought them terrible."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And do you think you will come to any harm by taking pains over yourself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By no means; rather that I shall get much benefit."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And on this single count that notion of yours is so much to the bad."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> True."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then, in the second place, observe the probability that it is false."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Is it probable that noble races should produce better natures, or not?", "st": "120e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly, noble races would."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And will not the well-born, provided they are well brought up, probably be perfected in virtue?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That must be so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then let us consider, by comparing our lot with theirs, whether the Spartan and Persian kings appear to be of inferior birth. Do we not know that the former are descendants of Hercules and the latter of Achaemenes, and that the line of Hercules and the line of Achaemenes go back to Perseus, son of Zeus?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, and mine, Socrates, to Eurysaces, and that of Eurysaces to Zeus!", "st": "121a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes, and mine, noble Alcibiades, to Daedalus, and Daedalus to Hephaestus, son of Zeus! But take the lines of those people, going back from them: you have a succession of kings reaching to Zeus—on the one hand, kings of Argos and Sparta; on the other, of Persia, which they have always ruled, and frequently Asia also, as at present; whereas we are private persons ourselves, and so were our fathers. And then, suppose that you had to make what show you could of your ancestors, and of Salamis as the native land of Eurysaces, or of Aegina as the home of the yet earlier Aeacus, to impress Artaxerxes, son of Xerxes, how you must expect to be laughed at! Why, I am afraid we are quite outdone by those persons in pride of birth and upbringing altogether. Or have you not observed how great are the advantages of the Spartan kings, and how their wives are kept under statutory ward of the ephors, in order that every possible precaution may be taken against the king being born of any but the Heracleidae? And the Persian king so far surpasses us that no one has a suspicion that he could have been born of anybody but the king before him; and hence the king’s wife has nothing to guard her except fear. When the eldest son, the heir to the throne, is born, first of all the king’s subjects who are in his palace have a feast, and then for ever after on that date the whole of Asia celebrates the king’s birthday with sacrifice and feasting: but when we are born, as the comic poet says, even the neighbors barely notice it, Alcibiades. After that comes the nurture of the child, not at the hands of a woman-nurse of little worth, but of the most highly approved eunuchs in the king’s service, who are charged with the whole tendance of the new-born child, and especially with the business of making him as handsome as possible by moulding his limbs into a correct shape; and while doing this they are in high honor. When the boys are seven years old they are given horses and have riding lessons, and they begin to follow the chase. And when the boy reaches fourteen years he is taken over by the royal tutors, as they call them there: these are four men chosen as the most highly esteemed among the Persians of mature age, namely, the wisest one, the justest one, the most temperate one, and the bravest one.", "st": "121b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> The first of these teaches him the magian lore of Zoroaster, son of Horomazes; and that is the worship of the gods: he teaches him also what pertains to a king. The justest teaches him to be truthful all his life long; the most temperate, not to be mastered by even a single pleasure, in order that he may be accustomed to be a free man and a veritable king, who is the master first of all that is in him, not the slave; while the bravest trains him to be fearless and undaunted, telling him that to be daunted is to be enslaved. But you, Alcibiades, had a tutor set over you by Pericles from amongst his servants, who was so old as to be the most useless of them, Zopyrus the Thracian. I might describe to you at length the nurture and education of your competitors, were it not too much of a task; and besides, what I have said suffices to show the rest that follows thereon. But about your birth, Alcibiades, or nurture or education, or about those of any other Athenian, one may say that nobody cares, unless it be some lover whom you chance to have. And again, if you chose to glance at the wealth, the luxury, the robes with sweeping trains, the anointings with myrrh, the attendant troops of menials, and all the other refinements of the Persians, you would be ashamed at your own case, on perceiving its inferiority to theirs. Should you choose, again, to look at the temperance and orderliness, the facility and placidity, the magnanimity and discipline, the courage and endurance, and the toil-loving, success-loving, honor-loving spirit of the Spartans, you would count yourself but a child in all these things. If again you regard wealth, and think yourself something in that way, I must not keep silence on this point either, if you are to realize where you stand. For in this respect you have only to look at the wealth of the Spartans, and you will perceive that our riches here are far inferior to theirs. Think of all the land that they have both in their own and in the Messenian country: not one of our estates could compete with theirs in extent and excellence, nor again in ownership of slaves, and especially of those of the helot class, nor yet of horses, nor of all the flocks and herds that graze in Messene. However, I pass over all these things: but there is more gold and silver privately held in Lacedaemon than in the whole of Greece; for during many generations treasure has been passing in to them from every part of Greece, and often from the barbarians also, but not passing out to anyone; and just as in the fable of Aesop, where the fox remarked to the lion on the direction of the footmarks, the traces of the money going into Lacedaemon are clear enough, but nowhere are any to be seen of it coming out;", "st": "122a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> so that one can be pretty sure that those people are the richest of the Greeks in gold and silver, and that among themselves the richest is the king; for the largest and most numerous receipts of the kind are those of the kings, and besides there is the levy of the royal tribute in no slight amount, which the Spartans pay to their kings. Now, the Spartan fortunes, though great compared with the wealth of other Greeks, are nought beside that of the Persians and their king. For I myself was once told by a trustworthy person, who had been up to their court, that he traversed a very large tract of excellent land, nearly a day’s journey, which the inhabitants called the girdle of the king’s wife, and another which was similarly called her veil; and many other fine and fertile regions reserved for the adornment of the consort; and each of these regions was named after some part of her apparel. So I imagine, if someone should say to the king’s mother Amestris, who was wife of Xerxes, The son of Deinomache intends to challenge your son; the mother’s dresses are worth perhaps fifty minae at the outside, while the son has under three hundred acres at Erchiae, she would wonder to what on earth this Alcibiades could be trusting, that he proposed to contend against Artaxerxes; and I expect she would remark— The only possible things that the man can be trusting to for his enterprise are industry and wisdom; for these are the only things of any account among the Greeks. Whereas if she were informed that this Alcibiades who is actually making such an attempt is, in the first place, as yet barely twenty years old, and secondly, altogether uneducated; and further, that when his lover tells him that he must first learn, and take pains over himself, and practise, before he enters on a contest with the king, he refuses, and says he will do very well as he is; I expect she would ask in surprise, On what, then, can the youngster rely? And if we told her, On beauty, stature, birth, wealth, and mental gifts, she would conclude we were mad, Alcibiades, when she compared the advantages of her own people in all these respects.", "st": "123a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I imagine that even Lampido, daughter of Leotychides and wife of Archidamus and mother of Agis, who have all been kings, would wonder in the same way, when she compared her people’s resources, at your intention of having a contest with her son despite your bad upbringing. And yet, does it not strike you as disgraceful that our enemies’ wives should have a better idea of the qualities that we need for an attempt against them than we have ourselves? Ah, my remarkable friend, listen to me and the Delphic motto, Know thyself; for these people are our competitors, not those whom you think; and there is nothing that will give us ascendancy over them save only pains and skill. If you are found wanting in these, you will be found wanting also in achievement of renown among Greeks and barbarians both; and of this I observe you to be more enamored than anyone else ever was of anything.", "st": "123e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well then, what are the pains that I must take, Socrates? Can you enlighten me? For I must say your words are remarkably like the truth.", "st": "124b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Yes, I can: but we must put our heads together, you know, as to the way in which we can improve ourselves to the utmost. For observe that when I speak of the need of being educated I am not referring only to you, apart from myself; since my case is identical with yours except in one point.", "st": "124c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is that?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> My guardian is better and wiser than your one, Pericles."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Who is he, Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> God, Alcibiades, who until this day would not let me converse with you; and trusting in him I say that through no other man but me will you attain to eminence."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You are jesting, Socrates.", "st": "124d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Perhaps; I am right, however, in saying that we need to take pains—all men rather badly, but we two very badly indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> As to me, you are not wrong."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor, I fear, as to myself either."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Then what can we do?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> There must be no crying off or skulking, my good friend."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, for that would indeed be unseemly, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> It would; so let us consider in common. Now tell me: we say, do we not, that we wish to be as good as possible?", "st": "124e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> In what excellence?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly that which is the aim of good men."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Good in what?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly, good in the management of affairs."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> What sort of affairs? Horsemanship?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because we should apply to horsemen?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, seamanship, do you mean?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because we should apply to seamen?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, what sort of thing? The business of what men?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of Athenian gentlemen."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Do you mean by gentlemen the intelligent or the unintelligent?", "st": "125a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> The intelligent."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And everyone is good in that wherein he is intelligent?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And bad wherein he is unintelligent?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then is the shoemaker intelligent in the making of foot-gear?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So he is good in that article?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, is not the shoemaker unintelligent in the making of clothes?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So he is bad in that?", "st": "125b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then, on this showing, the same man is both bad and good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, can you say that good men are also bad?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But whoever do you mean by the good?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I mean those who are able to rule in the city."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Not, I presume, over horses?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But over men?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> When they are sick?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Or at sea?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I say, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Or harvesting?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Doing nothing, or doing something?", "st": "125c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Doing something, I say."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Doing what? Try and let me know."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, men who do business with each other and make use of one another, as is our way of life in our cities."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you speak of ruling over men who make use of men?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Over boatswains who make use of rowers?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because that is the pilot’s distinction?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, do you mean ruling over men who are flute-players, and who lead the singing and make use of dancers?", "st": "125d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because, again, that is the chorus-teacher’s function?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But whatever do you mean by being able to rule over men who make use of men?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I mean ruling over men in the city who share in it as fellow-citizens, and do business with each other."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, what art is this? Suppose I should ask you over again, as I did just now, what art makes men know how to rule over fellow-sailors?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> The pilot’s."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what knowledge—to repeat what was said a moment ago—makes them rule over their fellow-singers?", "st": "125e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That which you just mentioned, the chorus-teacher’s."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, what do you call the knowledge of one’s fellow-citizens?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Good counsel, I should say, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, and is the pilot’s knowledge evil counsel?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Rather good counsel?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> So I should think, for the preservation of his passengers.", "st": "126a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Quite right. And now, for what is the good counsel of which you speak?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> For the better management and preservation of the city."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what is it that becomes present or absent when we get this better management and preservation? If, for example, you should ask me, What is it that becomes present or absent when the body is better managed and preserved? —I should reply, Health becomes present, and disease absent. Do not you think so too?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes.", "st": "126b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if, again, you asked me, What becomes present in a better condition of the eyes? —I should answer in just the same way, Sight becomes present, and blindness absent. So, in the case of the ears, deafness is caused to be absent, and hearing to be present, when they are improved and getting better treatment."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Correct."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, what is it that becomes present or absent when a state is improved and has better treatment and management?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To my mind, Socrates, friendship with one another will be there, while hatred and faction will be absent.", "st": "126c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now, by friendship do you mean agreement or disagreement?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Agreement."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what art is it that causes states to agree about numbers?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Arithmetic."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what of individuals? Is it not the same art?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And it makes each single person agree with himself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what art makes each of us agree with himself as to which is the longer, a span or a cubit? Is it not mensuration?", "st": "126d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And it makes both individuals and states agree with each other?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what about the balance? Is it not the same here too?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It is."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what is that agreement of which you speak, and about what? And what art secures it? And is it the same in an individual as in a state, when one agrees with oneself and with another?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Most likely."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, what is it? Do not flag in your answers, but do your best to tell me.", "st": "126e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I suppose I mean the friendship and agreement that you find when a father and mother love their son, and between brother and brother, and husband and wife."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then do you suppose, Alcibiades, that a husband can possibly agree with his wife about woolwork, when he does not understand it, and she does?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Oh, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor has he any need, since that is a woman’s pursuit."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Or again, could a woman agree with a man about soldiering, when she has not learnt it?", "st": "127a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Oh, no."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because, I expect you will say again, that is a man’s affair."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I would."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then, by your account, there are some pursuits belonging to women, and some to men?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So in these, at any rate, there is no agreement between men and women."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And hence no friendship either, if, as we said, friendship is agreement."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So women are not loved by men, in so far as they do their own work."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems not.", "st": "127b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor are men by women, in so far as they do theirs."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And states, therefore, are not well ordered in so far as each person does his own business?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think they are, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> How can you say that? Without the presence of friendship, which we say must be there if states are well ordered, as otherwise they are not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> But it seems to me that friendship arises among them just on that account—that each of the two parties does its own business."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> It was not so a moment since: but now, what do you mean this time? Does friendship arise where there is no agreement? And is it possible that agreement should arise where some know about the business, but others do not?", "st": "127c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Impossible."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And are they doing what is just or unjust, when each man does his own business?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is just, of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And when the citizens do what is just in the city, does not friendship arise among them?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Again I think that must be so, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then whatever do you mean by that friendship or agreement about which we must be wise and well-advised in order that we may be good men? For I am unable to learn either what it is, or in whom; since it appears that the same persons sometimes have it, and sometimes not, by your account.", "st": "127d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, by Heaven, Socrates, I do not even know what I mean myself, and I fear that for some time past I have lived unawares in a disgraceful condition."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But you must take heart. For had you perceived your plight at fifty, it would be hard for you to take pains with yourself; whereas here you are at the time of life when one ought to perceive it.", "st": "127e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Then what should one do on perceiving it, Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Answer the questions asked, Alcibiades: only do that, and with Heaven’s favor—if we are to put any trust in my divination—you and I shall both be in better case."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That shall be, so far as my answering can avail."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come then, what is taking pains over oneself — for we may perchance be taking, unawares, no pains over ourselves, though we think we are—and when does a man actually do it? Does he take pains over himself at the same time as over his own things?", "st": "128a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I at least believe so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, when does a man take pains over his feet? Is it when he takes pains over what belongs to his feet?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do not understand."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Is there anything you can name as belonging to the hand? For instance, does a ring belong to any other part of a man but the finger?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so the shoe also belongs to the foot, in the same way?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And likewise clothes and coverlets belong to the whole body?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes.", "st": "128b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now when we take pains over our shoes, we take pains over our feet?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do not quite understand, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, but, Alcibiades, you speak of taking proper pains over this or that matter, do you not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And do you call it proper pains when someone makes a thing better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what art makes shoes better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Shoe-making."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So by shoe-making we take pains over our shoes?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes.", "st": "128c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And over our foot too by shoe-making? Or by that art whereby we make feet better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By that art."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And is it not the same one for making our feet as for making the whole body better?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And is not that gymnastic?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Certainly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So by gymnastic we take pains over our foot, but by shoe-making over what belongs to our foot?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And by gymnastic over our hands, but by ring-engraving over what belongs to the hand?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And by gymnastic over the body, but by weaving and the rest over what belongs to the body?", "st": "128d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Absolutely so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then for taking pains over a thing itself and over what belongs to it we use different arts."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So when you take pains over your belongings you are not taking pains over yourself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Not at all."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For the arts, it seems, that one used for taking pains over oneself and over one’s belongings would not be the same."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come then, whatever kind of art can we use for taking pains over ourselves?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I cannot say."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, so much at least has been admitted, that it is not one which would help us to make a single one of our possessions better, but one which would help to make ourselves so?", "st": "128e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now, should we ever have known what art makes a shoe better, if we had not known a shoe?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Impossible."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor could we know what art makes rings better, if we had no cognizance of a ring."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> True."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, could we ever know what art makes the man himself better, if we were ignorant of what we are ourselves?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Impossible.", "st": "129a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, and is it an easy thing to know oneself, and was it a mere scamp who inscribed these words on the temple at Delphi; or is it a hard thing, and not a task for anybody?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I have often thought, Socrates, that it was for anybody; but often, too, that it was very hard."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But, Alcibiades, whether it is easy or not, here is the fact for us all the same: if we have that knowledge, we are like to know what pains to take over ourselves; but if we have it not, we never can."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Come then, in what way can the same-in-itself be discovered? For thus we may discover what we are ourselves; whereas if we remain in ignorance of it we must surely fail.", "st": "129b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Rightly spoken."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Steady, then, in Heaven’s name! To whom are you talking now? To me, are you not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I in turn to you?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then the talker is Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the hearer, Alcibiades?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And Socrates uses speech in talking?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course.", "st": "129c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you call talking and using speech the same thing, I suppose."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But the user and the thing he uses are different, are they not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How do you mean?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For instance, I suppose a shoemaker uses a round tool, and a square one, and others, when he cuts."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the cutter and user is quite different from what he uses in cutting?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And in the same way what the harper uses in harping will be different from the harper himself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, that is what I was asking just now—whether the user and what he uses are always, in your opinion, two different things.", "st": "129d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> They are."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then what are we to say of the shoemaker? Does he cut with his tools only, or with his hands as well?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> With his hands as well."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So he uses these also?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Does he use his eyes, too, in his shoe-making?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And we admit that the user and what he uses are different things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then the shoemaker and the harper are different from the hands and eyes that they use for their work?", "st": "129e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And man uses his whole body too?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And we said that the user and what he uses are different?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So man is different from his own body?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then whatever is man?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I cannot say."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Oh, but you can—that he is the user of the body."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the user of it must be the soul?", "st": "130a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It must."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And ruler?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Now, here is a remark from which no one, I think, can dissent."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> That man must be one of three things."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What things?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Soul, body, or both together as one whole."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Very well."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But yet we have admitted that what actually rules the body is man?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> We have.", "st": "130b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And does the body rule itself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> By no means."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Because we have said that it is ruled."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then that cannot be what we are seeking."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well then, does the combination of the two rule the body, so that we are to regard this as man?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Perhaps it is."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> The unlikeliest thing in the world: for if one of the two does not share in the rule, it is quite inconceivable that the combination of the two can be ruling."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> You are right."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But since neither the body nor the combination of the two is man, we are reduced, I suppose, to this: either man is nothing at all, or if something, he turns out to be nothing else than soul.", "st": "130c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Precisely so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, do you require some yet clearer proof that the soul is man?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, I assure you: I think it is amply proved."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if it is tolerably, though not exactly, we are content; exact knowledge will be ours later, when we have discovered the thing that we passed over just now because it would involve much consideration.", "st": "130d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is that?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> The point suggested in that remark a moment ago, that we should first consider the same-in-itself; but so far, instead of the same, we have been considering what each single thing is in itself. And perhaps we shall be satisfied with that: for surely we cannot say that anything has more absolute possession of ourselves than the soul."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And it is proper to take the view that you and I are conversing with each other, while we make use of words, by intercourse of soul with soul?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, that is just what we suggested a little while ago—that Socrates, in using words to talk with Alcibiades, is holding speech, not with your face, it would seem, but with Alcibiades—that is, with his soul.", "st": "130e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I believe so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then he who enjoins a knowledge of oneself bids us become acquainted with the soul."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> So it seems.", "st": "131a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And anyone who gets to know something belonging to the body knows the things that are his, but not himself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then no physician, in so far as he is a physician, knows himself, nor does any trainer, in so far as he is a trainer."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It seems not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And farmers, and craftsmen generally, are far from knowing themselves. For these people, it would seem, do not even know their own things, but only things still more remote than their own things, in respect of the arts which they follow; since they know but the things of the body, with which it is tended.", "st": "131b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So if knowing oneself is temperance, none of these people is temperate in respect of his art."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> None, I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And that is why these arts are held to be sordid, and no acquirements for a good man."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then once again, whoever tends his body tends his own things, but not himself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It looks rather like it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But whoever tends his money tends neither himself nor his own things, but only things yet more remote than his own things?", "st": "131c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So that the money-maker has ceased to do his own business."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Correct."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if anyone is found to be a lover of Alcibiades’ body, he has fallen in love, not with Alcibiades, but with something belonging to Alcibiades?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Your lover is rather he who loves your soul?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> He must be, apparently, by our argument."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And he who loves your body quits you, and is gone, as soon as its bloom is over?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Whereas he who loves your soul will not quit you so long as it makes for what is better?", "st": "131d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> So it seems."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And I am he who does not quit you, but remains with you when your body’s prime is over, and the rest have departed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, and I am glad of it, Socrates, and hope you will not go."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you must endeavor to be as handsome as you can."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, I shall endeavor."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> You see how you stand: Alcibiades, the son of Cleinias, it seems, neither had nor has any lover except one only, and that a cherished one, Socrates, the son of Sophroniscus and Phaenarete.", "st": "131e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> True."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And you said that I only just anticipated you in coming to you, for otherwise you would have come to me first for the purpose of inquiring why I am the only one who does not leave you?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, that was so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then the reason was that I was the only lover of you, whereas the rest were lovers of what is yours; and that is losing its charm, while you are beginning to bloom. So now, if you are not blighted and deformed by the Athenian people, I shall never forsake you. For my chiefest fear is of your being blighted by becoming a lover of the people, since many a good Athenian has come to that ere now. For fair of face is the people of great-hearted Erechtheus; but you should get a view of it stripped: so take the precaution that I recommend.", "st": "132a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What is it?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Exercise yourself first, my wonderful friend, in learning what you ought to know before entering on politics; you must wait till you have learnt, in order that you may be armed with an antidote and so come to no harm.", "st": "132b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Your advice seems to me good, Socrates; but try to explain in what way we can take pains over ourselves."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, we have made one step in advance; for there is a pretty fair agreement now as to what we are, whereas we were afraid we might fail of this and take pains, without knowing it, over something other than ourselves."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the next step, we see, is to take care of the soul, and look to that.", "st": "132c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> While handing over to others the care of our bodies and our coffers."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then how shall we obtain the most certain knowledge of it? For if we know that, it seems we shall know ourselves also. In Heaven’s name, do we fail to comprehend the wise words of the Delphic inscription, which we mentioned just now?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> With what intent do you say that, Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I will tell you what I suspect to be the real advice which the inscription gives us. I rather think there are not many illustrations of it to be found, but only in the case of sight.", "st": "132d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> What do you mean by that?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Consider in your turn: suppose that, instead of speaking to a man, it said to the eye of one of us, as a piece of advice See thyself, how should we apprehend the meaning of the admonition? Would it not be, that the eye should look at that by looking at which it would see itself?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Clearly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then let us think what object there is anywhere, by looking at which we can see both it and ourselves.", "st": "132e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Why, clearly, Socrates, mirrors and things of that sort."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Quite right. And there is also something of that sort in the eye that we see with?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And have you observed that the face of the person who looks into another’s eye is shown in the optic confronting him, as in a mirror, and we call this the pupil, for in a sort it is an image of the person looking?", "st": "133a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true.", "st": "133b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then an eye viewing another eye, and looking at the most perfect part of it, the thing wherewith it sees, will thus see itself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But if it looks at any other thing in man or at anything in nature but what resembles this, it will not see itself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then if an eye is to see itself, it must look at an eye, and at that region of the eye in which the virtue of an eye is found to occur; and this, I presume, is sight."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if the soul too, my dear Alcibiades, is to know herself, she must surely look at a soul, and especially at that region of it in which occurs the virtue of a soul—wisdom, and at any other part of a soul which resembles this?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I agree, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And can we find any part of the soul that we can call more divine than this, which is the seat of knowledge and thought?", "st": "133c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> We cannot."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then this part of her resembles God, and whoever looks at this, and comes to know all that is divine, will gain thereby the best knowledge of himself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And self-knowledge we admitted to be temperance."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So if we have no knowledge of ourselves and no temperance, shall we be able to know our own belongings, good or evil?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How can that be, Socrates?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For I expect it seems impossible to you that without knowing Alcibiades you should know that the belongings of Alcibiades are in fact his.", "st": "133d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Impossible indeed, upon my word."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor could we know that our belongings are ours if we did not even know ourselves?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How could we?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so, if we did not so much as know our belongings, we could not know the belongings of our belongings either?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently not."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then we were not quite correct in admitting just now that there are people who, without knowing themselves, know their belongings, while others know their belongings’ belongings. For it seems to be the function of one man and one art to discern all three— himself, his belongings, and the belongings of his belongings.", "st": "133e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It looks like it."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And anyone who is ignorant of his belongings will be similarly ignorant, I suppose, of the belongings of others."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Quite so."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if ignorant of others’ affairs, he will be ignorant also of the affairs of states."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> He must be."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then such a man can never be a statesman."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> No, nor an economist either."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed.", "st": "134a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Nor will he know what he is doing."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, I agree."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And will not he who does not know make mistakes?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> To be sure."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And when he makes mistakes, will he not do ill both in private and in public?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And doing ill he will be wretched?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, very."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And what of those for whom he is doing so?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> They will be wretched also."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then it is impossible to be happy if one is not temperate and good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Impossible."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So it is the bad men who are wretched.", "st": "134b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes, very."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And hence it is not he who has made himself rich that is relieved of wretchedness, but he who has made himself temperate."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So it is not walls or warships or arsenals that cities need, Alcibiades, if they are to be happy, nor numbers, nor size, without virtue."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> No, indeed."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And if you are to manage the city’s affairs properly and honorably, you must impart virtue to the citizens."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But could one possibly impart a thing that one had not?", "st": "134c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> How, indeed?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then you or anyone else who is to be governor and curator, not merely of himself and his belongings in private, but of the state and its affairs, must first acquire virtue himself."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Hence it is not licence or authority for doing what one pleases that you have to secure to yourself or the state, but justice and temperance."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For you and the state, if you act justly and temperately, will act so as to please God.", "st": "134d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Naturally."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And, as we were saying in what went before, you will act with your eyes turned on what is divine and bright."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well, and looking thereon you will behold and know both yourselves and your good."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And so you will act aright and well?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Well now, if you act in this way, I am ready to warrant that you must be happy.", "st": "134e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> And I can rely on your warranty."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> But if you act unjustly, with your eyes on the godless and dark, the probability is that your acts will resemble these through your ignorance of yourselves."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is probable."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> For if a man, my dear Alcibiades, is at liberty to do what he pleases, but is lacking in mind, what is the probable result to him personally, or to the state as well? For instance, if he is sick and at liberty to do what he pleases—without a medical mind, but with a despot’s power which prevents anyone from even reproving him—what will be the result? Will not his health, in all likelihood, be shattered?", "st": "135a"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Again, in a ship, if a man were at liberty to do what he chose, but were devoid of mind and excellence in navigation, do you perceive what must happen to him and his fellow-sailors?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do: they must all perish."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And in just the same way, if a state, or any office or authority, is lacking in excellence or virtue, it will be overtaken by failure?", "st": "135b"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> It must."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then it is not despotic power, my admirable Alcibiades, that you ought to secure either to yourself or to the state, if you would be happy, but virtue."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> That is true."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And before getting virtue, to be governed by a superior is better than to govern, for a man as well as a child."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the better is also nobler?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And the nobler more becoming?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Of course."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then it becomes a bad man to be a slave, since it is better.", "st": "135c"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> So vice is a thing that becomes a slave."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Apparently."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And virtue becomes a free man."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Yes."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And we should shun, my good friend, all slavishness?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Most certainly, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> And do you now perceive how you stand? Are you on the side of the free, or not?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I think I perceive only too clearly."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Then do you know how you may escape from the condition in which you now find yourself? Let us not give it a name, where a handsome person is concerned!"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> I do.", "st": "135d"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> How?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> If it be your wish, Socrates."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> That is not well said, Alcibiades."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, what should I say?"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> If it be God’s will."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Then I say it. And yet I say this besides, that we are like to make a change in our parts, Socrates, so that I shall have yours and you mine. For from this day onward it must be the case that I am your attendant, and you have me always in attendance on you."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> Ah, generous friend! So my love will be just like a stork; for after hatching a winged love in you it is to be cherished in return by its nestling.", "st": "135e"}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Alc:<\/span> Well, that is the position, and I shall begin here and now to take pains over justice."}, {"sp": "N", "t": "<span class=\"speaker-label\">Soc:<\/span> I should like to think you will continue to do so; yet I am apprehensive, not from any distrust of your nature, but in view of the might of the state, lest it overcome both me and you."}]);})()